    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A dua is a personal prayer, calling on God in your own words. The Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, named three whose dua is never rejected.",
      "video": "main/broll6/three-duas-answered/1-intro.mp4",
      "videoDuration": 13,
      "holdSeconds": 0.4,
      "dim": 0.44,
      "voiceSettings": {
        "stability": 0.6,
        "style": 0.16,
        "similarity_boost": 0.85,
        "speed": 0.99
      },
      "arabicText": "ثَلاَثَةٌ لاَ تُرَدُّ دَعْوَتُهُمْ",
      "foot": "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3598; also Sunan Ibn Majah 1752. Hasan."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The first is the fasting person, going without food and drink for God from dawn to sunset. Their prayer is answered, all the way until they break their fast.",
      "video": "main/broll6/three-duas-answered/2-point-one.mp4",
      "videoDuration": 13,
      "holdSeconds": 0.4,
      "dim": 0.44,
      "voiceSettings": {
        "stability": 0.6,
        "style": 0.16,
        "similarity_boost": 0.85,
        "speed": 0.99
      },
      "arabicText": "الصَّائِمُ حَتَّى يُفْطِرَ",
      "foot": "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3598; Sunan Ibn Majah 1752. Hasan."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The second is the just leader, the one who holds power over others and rules them with fairness.",
      "video": "main/broll6/three-duas-answered/3-point-two.mp4",
      "videoDuration": 13,
      "holdSeconds": 0.4,
      "dim": 0.44,
      "voiceSettings": {
        "stability": 0.6,
        "style": 0.16,
        "similarity_boost": 0.85,
        "speed": 0.99
      },
      "arabicText": "وَالإِمَامُ الْعَادِلُ",
      "foot": "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3598; Sunan Ibn Majah 1752. Hasan."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The third is the wronged, the one treated unjustly and left with nowhere to turn but God.",
      "video": "main/broll6/three-duas-answered/4-point-three.mp4",
      "videoDuration": 13,
      "holdSeconds": 0.4,
      "dim": 0.44,
      "voiceSettings": {
        "stability": 0.6,
        "style": 0.16,
        "similarity_boost": 0.85,
        "speed": 0.99
      },
      "arabicText": "وَدَعْوَةُ الْمَظْلُومِ",
      "foot": "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3598; Sunan Ibn Majah 1752. Hasan."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "God raises the prayer of the wronged high above the clouds, and opens the gates of heaven for it.",
      "video": "main/broll6/three-duas-answered/5-deepen.mp4",
      "videoDuration": 13,
      "holdSeconds": 0.4,
      "dim": 0.44,
      "voiceSettings": {
        "stability": 0.6,
        "style": 0.16,
        "similarity_boost": 0.85,
        "speed": 0.99
      },
      "arabicText": "يَرْفَعُهَا اللَّهُ فَوْقَ الْغَمَامِ",
      "foot": "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3598. Hasan."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And God says: by My might, I will surely help you, even if it takes time.",
      "video": "main/broll6/three-duas-answered/6-promise.mp4",
      "videoDuration": 13,
      "holdSeconds": 0.4,
      "dim": 0.44,
      "voiceSettings": {
        "stability": 0.6,
        "style": 0.16,
        "similarity_boost": 0.85,
        "speed": 0.99
      },
      "arabicText": "وَعِزَّتِي لأَنْصُرَنَّكِ وَلَوْ بَعْدَ حِينٍ",
      "foot": "Jami at-Tirmidhi 3598. Hasan."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "So if you fast, if you lead fairly, or if you are wronged, know that your voice is heard.",
